<title>USA: HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to Watch - July 7.</title>
<headline>HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to Watch - July 7.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>-- Integrated Health Services Inc and Rotech MedicalCorp have agreed to merge in a stock swap worth $615 million. Integrated Health closed Thursday at 38-15/16, and Rotech closed at 18-7/8.</p>
<p>-- The New York investment firm Welsh, Carson, Anderson &amp; Stowe is among the companies vying for CompuServe Corp, the Wall Street Journal reported. H&amp;R Block is trying to sell its 80 percent stake in CompuServe.  </p>
<p>CompuServe closed at 10-3/4. H&amp;R Block closed at 32-3/4.</p>
<p>-- British Airways cabin crew plan three-day strikes starting Wednesday. The company's ADRs closed at 115-11/16.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street Desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
